<title>USA: Enron Oil &amp; Gas Q2 shr falls.</title>
<headline>Enron Oil &amp; Gas Q2 shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.16		    $0.30</p>
<p> Net			   24.6		     47.6</p>
<p> Oper revs		  171.8		    197.1</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   157.5		    159.9</p>
<p>			 6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.30		    $0.46</p>
<p> Net			   47.6		     73.5</p>
<p> Oper revs		  352.4		    356.1</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   158.2		    159.9</p>
<p>(All data above in millions except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net income, discretionary cash flow, and net operating revenues were lower primarily due to lower gains/proceeds from property sales on lower other marketing net revenue.</p>
<p>Discretionary cash flow was $123.9 million in the second quarter of 1997 compared with $197.1 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Enron Oil &amp; Gas is majority owned by Enron Corp.</p>
<p>Period ended June 30.</p>
</text>
